  "claim_boundary": "This development-tier protocol admits only the source-v5 synthetic Product Horizon campaign input after exact owner replay, public-to-sealed trajectory joining, all 5,376-by-3 action-conditioned branch commitments, and full-string exclusion against source-v3, source-v4, and the closed adaptive reader-input registry existing at this protocol freeze. The registry union contains the development reader table plus the attempt03 table; source-v3, source-v4, and qualification-v5 are mechanically verified subsets of that development table, while qualification-v5 remains lineage-only. Any future adaptive reader input requires a new protocol identity. Exact string disjointness is not semantic novelty, DGP independence, statistical independence, or unseen evidence. Materialization is create-only and writes the manifest last after a second full semantic rebuild and byte comparison; this is cooperative live ordering, not power-loss durability or process-security independence. A future consumer must invoke read-only validate-existing with externally supplied protocol and artifact identities. Random draws remain action-specific because selected_action enters the environment hash, so this is not a common-random-number design. Admission does not freeze or execute a campaign, establish runtime preaction or postaction ordering, prove forecast arm, scope, or call-order blinding, materialize a source-v5 embedding table, fit or qualify a reader, export theta, prove geometric reachability or PE-credit achievability, run a model, CUDA, or rehearsal, or authorize formal, unseen, integrated, four-able, human, or production evidence. The 112 roots are synthetic units, not people. This Product Horizon artifact inherits no estimand, N, protocol identity, or evidence claim from A1 reactive-source qualification or the A2 MSC budget line."
